  "about": "The one particle pool's kinds (docs/render/MATERIALS.md, 'Effects'). A particle has a position, a speed, a size, a life and a tint; a kind says how it looks and moves over its life. Keys: sizeFrom, sizeTo: its size at birth and death, times the size it was made with. colours: [from, middle, to] (over 1 is fine: flames are bright, and a glow's light is what the bloom picks up); mid: when in its life (0..1) it is the middle colour. alpha: how much it covers at most; fadeIn: the share of its life it takes to appear; fadePow: how fast it goes (1 even, 3 late fall). glow: 0 smoke, which covers what is behind it, 1 light, which only adds to it. lit: 1 takes the sky's light, 0 its own. gravity: m/s2 down (below 0 it rises); drag: how much speed it loses a second; turbulence: m/s2 of drift. stretch: seconds of travel drawn as a streak (0: a round puff).",
